1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,934
Taurus runs several Claude Code agents as terminal tabs in one window.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,737
Every tab is a real console process, started in a folder

3
00:00:10,737 --> 00:00:14,140
you pick, and it keeps running while you look away.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,500
The window holds nothing that matters.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,868
It asks the machine half for work by

6
00:00:21,868 --> 00:00:25,092
name, and there are seventy-three of those names.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,377
Starting a tab makes a real console process on

8
00:00:32,377 --> 00:00:35,682
the machine, and a screen buffer in the page.

9
00:00:35,682 --> 00:00:37,150
One tab, two halves.

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,789
What the agent prints comes back on its own channel, and the page draws it.

11
00:00:45,789 --> 00:00:48,279
Thirteen channels carry the two halves.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,508
The open tabs and the history are written to seven plain files outside the program.

13
00:00:58,508 --> 00:01:00,964
They outlive any rewrite of the code.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,643
Nothing checks that the two sides agree on a name.

15
00:01:08,643 --> 00:01:12,140
Rename one alone and it fails at a button press.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,556
Three road signs: a command wired to nothing, a trail

17
00:01:18,556 --> 00:01:22,314
nobody listens for, and one word that names four things.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,412
Open the catalog, then one card.

19
00:01:27,412 --> 00:01:29,145
That is the whole rule.
